---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import personal from '../data/personal.json';

const link =
  'text-csii-ochre underline decoration-csii-gold underline-offset-4 hover:text-csii-brown dark:text-csii-gold dark:hover:text-struct-sand';
const h2Class = 'mt-10 font-serif text-xl font-medium tracking-tight';
const pClass = 'mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed';
const ulClass = 'mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Siratee Lertsubthaworn"
  description="Privacy Policy for sirateelert.github.io: what information is processed, why, and the rights available under Thai data protection law."
>
  <Header />

  <main id="main" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-14">
    <p class="mb-1 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-csii-ochre dark:text-csii-gold">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">Last updated: 30 September 2026</p>

    <article aria-label="Privacy Policy">
      <h2 class={h2Class}>1. Scope and Controller</h2>
      <p class={pClass}>
        This policy applies to sirateelert.github.io (the &ldquo;Site&rdquo;), operated by {personal.fullName}
        ({personal.location}), who acts as the data controller for personal data processed through the Site.
        The Site is a personal academic and professional portfolio.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2Class}>2. Information Processed</h2>
      <ul class={ulClass}>
        <li>
          <strong>Information you send directly.</strong> If you contact the author by email or telephone, the
          information you provide (such as your name, contact details and message content) is processed in order
          to respond.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hosting and technical data.</strong> The Site is served from GitHub Pages. Like most web hosts,
          the hosting provider may process technical data such as IP addresses and browser information in server
          logs. Please see GitHub&rsquo;s own privacy statement for details.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics.</strong> Where enabled, the Site uses Umami Cloud to collect aggregate,
          privacy-oriented usage statistics (for example, pages viewed and referrer). Umami is designed not to
          use cookies or to track individuals across websites.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Web fonts.</strong> The Site loads typefaces from Google Fonts. When a page loads, your browser
          sends a request, including your IP address, to Google&rsquo;s servers.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Theme preference.</strong> Your light or dark mode choice is stored in your browser&rsquo;s local
          storage. It stays on your device and is not transmitted to the author.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class={h2Class}>3. Purposes and Legal Bases</h2>
      <p class={pClass}>
        Personal data is processed to respond to enquiries, to operate and secure the Site, and to understand
        aggregate usage so that content can be improved. Under Thailand&rsquo;s Personal Data Protection Act B.E.
        2562 (2019) (&ldquo;PDPA&rdquo;), the bases relied upon are your consent (where you initiate contact) and
        the legitimate interests of the author in operating a secure and useful Site, balanced against your rights.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2Class}>4. Automated Tools and Generative AI</h2>
      <p class={pClass}>
        Personal data or non-public information that you send to the author is not submitted to automated
        third-party large language model services unless strict compliance measures are in place, including
        appropriate authorisation and compliance with applicable data protection law. See the
        <a href="/#governance" class={link}>Generative AI &amp; Tooling Governance</a> statement.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2Class}>5. Retention</h2>
      <p class={pClass}>
        Correspondence is retained only as long as necessary to handle your enquiry and any reasonable follow-up,
        and is then deleted or anonymised. Analytics and hosting logs are retained according to the policies of
        the respective providers.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2Class}>6. Disclosure and International Transfers</h2>
      <p class={pClass}>
        Personal data is not sold. It may be processed by service providers acting for the Site (hosting,
        analytics and font delivery), some of which operate outside Thailand. Where this occurs, processing is
        subject to those providers&rsquo; own safeguards and terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2Class}>7. Your Rights</h2>
      <p class={pClass}>Subject to the conditions and exceptions of the PDPA, you may have the right to:</p>
      <ul class={ulClass}>
        <li>access and obtain a copy of your personal data;</li>
        <li>request rectification of inaccurate or incomplete data;</li>
        <li>request erasure or restriction of processing;</li>
        <li>object to processing and request data portability;</li>
        <li>withdraw consent at any time, without affecting processing already carried out; and</li>
        <li>lodge a complaint with the Personal Data Protection Committee of Thailand.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class={h2Class}>8. Security</h2>
      <p class={pClass}>
        Reasonable technical and organisational measures are used to protect personal data. No method of
        transmission or storage is completely secure, and absolute security cannot be guaranteed.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2Class}>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p class={pClass}>
        This policy may be updated from time to time. The date of the latest revision appears at the top of this
        page.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2Class}>10. Contact</h2>
      <p class={pClass}>
        For privacy enquiries or to exercise your rights, contact
        <a href={`mailto:${personal.email}`} class={link}>{personal.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>

    <p class="mt-12 text-sm">
      <a href="/" class={link}>&larr; Return to home page</a>
    </p>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
